PYTHON LAB 2 - FIXED ARRAYS AND PRINT

Create /tmp/seq.py:

  a = [1, 2, 3]
  print(a)
  print(len(a))
  b = bytes([65, 66])
  print(b)

Run: python /tmp/seq.py
Expected: one representation of [1,2,3], then length 3, then
the byte-sequence display. Exact rendering is interpreter-specific;
compare the observed representation rather than assuming CPython repr.

Lists and bytes are fixed-size integer sequences (<=64 elements).
No slicing, methods, .append(), enumerate(), imports or dynamic
memory allocation. Strings share a small fixed storage pool.
